WEBVTT

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.254
by suspending the fluid in 
their inner ears

00:03:02.254 --> 00:03:03.766
which coordinates balance.

00:03:03.766 --> 00:03:05.327
But the bigger potential danger

00:03:05.327 --> 00:03:06.393
– and thrill –

00:03:06.393 --> 00:03:09.516
comes from what ride designers 
call airtime.

00:03:09.516 --> 00:03:13.049
This is when riders typically
experience seat separation,

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:14.840
and, without the proper precautions,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.943
ejection.

00:03:15.943 --> 00:03:18.654
The numerous belts and harnesses 
of modern coasters

00:03:18.654 --> 00:03:20.612
have largely solved this issue,

00:03:20.612 --> 00:03:24.059
but the passenger’s ever-changing position
can make it difficult

00:03:24.059 --> 00:03:26.926
to determine what needs to be 
strapped down.

00:03:26.926 --> 00:03:29.718
Fortunately, modern ride designers
are well aware

00:03:29.718 --> 00:03:31.416
